<title>SWITZERLAND: Swisslog buys German Transnorm.</title>
<headline>Swisslog buys German Transnorm.</headline>
<dateline>AARAU, Switzerland 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swisslog Holding AG said it had signed a letter of intent to purchase the German  Transnorm Systems Group, based in Harsum near Hanover for an undisclosed amount.</p>
<p>Juhani Anttila, Swisslog chief executive, was quoted in a statement as saying that Transnorm had 1996 sales of 75 million German marks and was active in the light goods conveyeing business.</p>
<p>Transnorm has subsidiaries in the United Kingdom, the U.S., the Netherlands, France and Malaysia.</p>
<p>Anttila said Swisslog's objective in acquiring Transnorm was to strenghten Swisslog's presence in Germany and gain a foothold in selected key industries in the growing logistics market in the U.S.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
